Package: ASCENT
Type: Package
Title: Accelerated Single-Cell ENhancer-Target Gene Linking
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Duc", "Nguyen", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "ngocduc.nguyen@childrens.harvard.edu"),
    person("Saori", "Sakaue", role = "ctb", comment = "Original SCENT implementation"),
    person("Shakson", "Isaac", role = "ctb", comment = "Original SCENT implementation"))
Description: Rcpp-accelerated reimplementation of SCENT (Single-Cell ENhancer Target)
    for linking ATAC-seq peaks to target genes using single-cell multimodal data.
    Uses Poisson or Negative Binomial regression with empirical p-values via
    iterative bootstrapping. Parallelized across peak-gene pairs using OpenMP
    with efficient sparse matrix access from C++.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Depends:
    R (>= 3.5.0),
    methods
Imports:
    Rcpp,
    Matrix,
    data.table,
    stringr,
    Hmisc
LinkingTo:
    Rcpp,
    RcppArmadillo
SystemRequirements: GNU make, bedtools, C++11
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
Encoding: UTF-8
